title: Field editors
intro: Fields that used to take something typed from memory now have editors of their own: items, flags and kinds picked from what the game has, dice built, points listed, tiles clicked off the tileset, clips and directions.
project: TopDown | Field Kit
write: Tiles/hex.png | hex-tilemaps/hex.png

chapter: Names it knows | Items, flags and kinds
select: Vault Door
explain: field:Switch.Key | Key | The vault's lock takes an item. It used to be a name typed from memory; now it's picked from the items the game gives, here the key a pickup puts in the player's inventory.
pick: Switch.Key = Key
expectvalue: Vault Door.Switch.Key = Key
expectflagged: Switch.Key = none
explain: field:Switch.Needs Flag | Needs Flag | Flags work the same way: the list has every flag a trigger, a dialogue or a script sets, and the word not in front of each, for while it isn't set.

chapter: Dice | A roll built, not typed
select: Bat
explain: field:DamageOnTouch.Amount Roll | Amount Roll | The bat's bite can roll dice. Type them if you like, or build them: how many, how many sides, and what's added.
editorset: DamageOnTouch.Amount Roll:count = 2
choose: DamageOnTouch.Amount Roll:sides = 4
editorset: DamageOnTouch.Amount Roll:plus = 1
expectvalue: Bat.DamageOnTouch.AmountRoll = 2d4+1
explain: editor:DamageOnTouch.Amount Roll:summary | What it rolls | Underneath, what it rolls: three to nine, six on average.

chapter: Points and directions | Rows, a compass and knobs
create: Empty
rename: Lift
add: Mover
explain: field:Mover.Points | Points | A mover's points were x and y pairs typed with semicolons between them. Now each is a row, with Add to put one on the end.
click: editor:Mover.Points:add
editorset: Mover.Points:y:2 = 3
expectvalue: Lift.Mover.Points = 4 0; 8 3
add: Shooter
explain: field:Shooter.Direction | Direction | Which way a shooter fires has a compass of the eight ways beside its numbers.
click: editor:Shooter.Direction:way:Up
expectvalue: Lift.Shooter.Direction.X = 0
expectvalue: Lift.Shooter.Direction.Y = 1
menu: View > Distance Handles
explain: handle:Shooter.Direction | In the Scene view | With distance handles out, the direction is an arrow to drag round, and offsets get knobs too, like where its shots appear.
vector: Ctrl+Shooter.Direction = -1, 0
expectvalue: Lift.Shooter.Direction.X = -1
expectvalue: Lift.Shooter.Direction.Y = 0

chapter: Tiles | Picked off the tileset
create: Tilemap
pickimage: Tilemap.Image = Tiles/hex.png
set: Tilemap.Columns = 4
explain: field:Tilemap.Background Tiles | Background Tiles | Tile numbers were the hardest thing to type from memory. Open the tileset beside them and click the tiles instead.
click: editor:Tilemap.Background Tiles:tiles
click: editor:Tilemap.Background Tiles:tile:1
click: editor:Tilemap.Background Tiles:tile:2
expectvalue: Tilemap.Tilemap.BackgroundTiles = 1, 2
click: editor:Tilemap.Animated Tiles:add
expectvalue: Tilemap.Tilemap.AnimatedTiles = 0-3 @4
explain: field:Tilemap.Animated Tiles | Animated Tiles | A run of animated tiles is a row too, from one tile to another at so many frames a second, with its frames shown.
click: editor:Tilemap.Auto Tiles:add
expectvalue: Tilemap.Tilemap.AutoTiles = 0-15
choose: Tilemap.More Tilesets:add = Tiles/hex.png
expectvalue: Tilemap.Tilemap.MoreTilesets = Tiles/hex.png 4x1

chapter: Clips | Rows, and the one it starts with
create: Sprite
rename: Hero
add: Animation
explain: field:Animation.Clips | Clips | An animation's clips were a line of names, frame ranges, speeds and the word once. Each is a row now, and the Clip Editor button shows them playing.
click: editor:Animation.Clips:add
editorset: Animation.Clips:name:1 = Run
expectvalue: Hero.Animation.Clips = Run 0-3
choose: Animation.Clip:choice = Run
expectvalue: Hero.Animation.Clip = Run
explain: field:Animation.Clip | Clip | The clip it starts with is picked from its own clips, so a typo can't slip in.
say: Every one of these is an undo step, and agents get the same choices through the editor's tools.
